Subject: The shared crates by name, at the copy of hyper-raft beside the bus
Why: Focal builds its bus against its own snapshots of hyper-raft's crates (vendor/hyper-* in Focal's tree). Quiver takes hyper-raft once, at the revision the bus takes (vendor/hyper-raft), and kiln holds one copy of each hyper-light product: the bus names the shared crates as from crates.io, and the root manifest of whoever builds it (Quiver's, or kiln's) points each name at its one copy with [patch.crates-io].

